      "local_deviation": "A Local implementation may manage local agent teammates; human invitation and organization membership actions must remain structurally unavailable when no cloud membership authority exists.",
      "judgment_rationale": "The Web Team page combines project human membership with project-scoped agent teammates. Its UserManager lists, updates and removes project members, but the visible invitation form sends POST /tenants/{tenant_id}/invitations through invitationService rather than adding a project member. Invitation therefore requires tenant-admin authority, while role changes and removal retain project-admin authority. Desktop now has a real production loader, App binding and revision-bound Cloud authority, but ProjectKnowledgePage only renders the member and Agent teammate lists and exposes no invitation, role, removal or start-chat control. Cloud is therefore partial with only view, list-members and list-agent-teammates. Local uses the same real route but workbenchCapabilityClient deliberately treats the static Local result as a renderer declaration, so it remains closed with local_project_team_authority_unavailable and no action authority."
