      "judgment_rationale": "Memory list, creation, detail, client-side JSON export, copy-link and reprocessing are one canonical project knowledge capability. The visible detail-page control uses navigator.clipboard to copy window.location.href; the routed production pages do not call the memory-share APIs, so no server sharing authority is claimed. Project viewers can read but cannot create memories; creation requires a project contributor. The production Web page has no memory-import action. Desktop now has a real production loader, App binding, typed client, controller and revision-bound Cloud authority, but ProjectKnowledgePage only renders the memory list and exposes no create, update, delete, reprocess, export or copy-link interaction. Cloud therefore retains only view and list and remains partial. Local binds the same native route but its renderer-declared static result is closed to local_project_memories_authority_unavailable until a sidecar observation exists."
